{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\_cls6_jpg\\eng\\132.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "A Subject Complement", "conf": 0.884, "box": [[124, 191], [409, 188], [409, 218], [124, 221]]}, {"text": "Example:", "conf": 0.854, "box": [[125, 235], [232, 235], [232, 263], [125, 263]]}, {"text": "My favourite was visiting the tranquil room.", "conf": 0.93, "box": [[123, 275], [622, 277], [622, 310], [123, 308]]}, {"text": "(\"Visiting\" is a subject complement. It completes the linking verb \"was\" and renames the", "conf": 0.931, "box": [[120, 320], [1155, 319], [1155, 351], [120, 352]]}, {"text": "subject, making it a subject complement.)", "conf": 0.908, "box": [[120, 361], [599, 363], [599, 396], [120, 394]]}, {"text": "1 Underline the gerunds in each sentence below and identify their functions.", "conf": 0.903, "box": [[117, 421], [1084, 421], [1084, 450], [117, 450]]}, {"text": "Walking the cat is my regular routine.", "conf": 0.887, "box": [[119, 477], [579, 479], [579, 509], [119, 507]]}, {"text": "I particularly enjoy travelling.", "conf": 0.917, "box": [[117, 532], [480, 534], [480, 563], [117, 561]]}, {"text": "Iamsotiredof climbing!", "conf": 0.855, "box": [[124, 588], [438, 588], [438, 615], [124, 615]]}, {"text": "Lately,shehasbeenhavingtroublesleeping.", "conf": 0.923, "box": [[118, 641], [663, 641], [663, 671], [118, 671]]}, {"text": "Drawing would be a good activity for you.", "conf": 0.849, "box": [[117, 697], [627, 695], [627, 725], [117, 727]]}, {"text": "Sleeping is our first priority.", "conf": 0.927, "box": [[115, 752], [464, 751], [464, 780], [115, 781]]}, {"text": "My favourite pastime is reading.", "conf": 0.884, "box": [[113, 806], [514, 804], [514, 835], [113, 837]]}, {"text": "Washing clothes will have to wait until Sunday.", "conf": 0.865, "box": [[113, 862], [682, 858], [683, 888], [113, 892]]}, {"text": "Listening to music is a remedy for loneliness.", "conf": 0.904, "box": [[115, 919], [659, 913], [659, 943], [115, 949]]}, {"text": "2 Make sentencesusing the following gerunds.", "conf": 0.911, "box": [[103, 971], [698, 962], [699, 994], [104, 1003]]}, {"text": "Gerund", "conf": 0.855, "box": [[366, 1025], [461, 1025], [461, 1056], [366, 1056]]}, {"text": "Functions", "conf": 0.898, "box": [[135, 1029], [259, 1027], [260, 1058], [136, 1060]]}, {"text": "Sentences", "conf": 0.843, "box": [[767, 1021], [901, 1021], [901, 1048], [767, 1048]]}, {"text": "As Subject of", "conf": 0.887, "box": [[132, 1079], [292, 1077], [292, 1108], [132, 1110]]}, {"text": "Finding", "conf": 0.803, "box": [[362, 1083], [455, 1089], [453, 1124], [360, 1119]]}, {"text": "a Verb", "conf": 0.837, "box": [[129, 1112], [212, 1112], [212, 1143], [129, 1143]]}, {"text": "As Object of", "conf": 0.888, "box": [[132, 1156], [280, 1156], [280, 1187], [132, 1187]]}, {"text": "Knowing", "conf": 0.873, "box": [[359, 1162], [466, 1166], [465, 1200], [358, 1196]]}, {"text": "a Verb", "conf": 0.779, "box": [[128, 1191], [209, 1188], [210, 1217], [129, 1220]]}, {"text": "As Object of", "conf": 0.91, "box": [[130, 1230], [279, 1228], [279, 1259], [130, 1261]]}, {"text": "Seeing", "conf": 0.853, "box": [[356, 1240], [442, 1243], [441, 1277], [355, 1275]]}, {"text": "a Preposition", "conf": 0.906, "box": [[127, 1265], [285, 1263], [285, 1293], [127, 1295]]}, {"text": "As Subject", "conf": 0.867, "box": [[131, 1307], [254, 1307], [254, 1337], [131, 1337]]}, {"text": "Falling", "conf": 0.854, "box": [[355, 1317], [439, 1320], [437, 1355], [353, 1351]]}, {"text": "Complement", "conf": 0.859, "box": [[131, 1342], [282, 1342], [282, 1369], [131, 1369]]}, {"text": "Writing", "conf": 0.701, "box": [[153, 1409], [288, 1417], [285, 1459], [150, 1451]]}, {"text": "The poem describes a passion for work. You can use poetry to describe various other things or", "conf": 0.941, "box": [[97, 1486], [1188, 1471], [1188, 1507], [98, 1522]]}, {"text": "objects or places. Try to write a simple poem describing any of your favourite objects or place.", "conf": 0.93, "box": [[99, 1524], [